{
  "_note": "ARTBOARD / STATE-MACHINE / ANIMATION SELECTION and its refusals. THE LAW. (1) With no attributes the fold takes the file's DEFAULT artboard (the flagged one, else the first) and that artboard's first state machine; with no machine it falls back to the first linear animation; with neither it is `idle`, which is legal — a static artboard is a drawing. (2) `stateMachine` and `animation` together is a CONFLICT, refused by name. A silent precedence rule is the bug an author never finds. (3) Every miss is `not_found` with a message naming what was asked for and where it was looked up: a missing artboard or machine must never render a blank box (plan §7). (4) A refusal is TOTAL — artboard, machine and animation all read null and the mode is `idle` — so a renderer can never half-mount a selection it was told to reject. (5) A blank attribute is an absent attribute; a name is otherwise exact, trimmed but never case-folded, because artboard names are authored strings. Function: riveSelection(manifest, attrs) on all three.",
